From 09d3c46ae0c23d663988aaf913560a0e20f08a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:09:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel behaviours: fixes from a review

- an empty batch whose fields are null (for example the data of empty
  vectors, on a process without any point of a material) was rejected as
  invalid;
- invalid computation options of a finite strain behaviour gave an
  integration failure at every point, which leads a calling code to
  reduce the time step indefinitely. They are rejected for the whole
  batch (status -2);
- the initialize functions and the post-processings overwrote the time
  step scaling factors proposed by the integration;
- the output status is complete if an exception is thrown before the
  batch data are checked;
- SYCL backend, `automatic` data transfer policy: the copied extents of
  the thermodynamic forces and of the tangent operators used the maximal
  sizes instead of the sizes selected by the computation options (values
  read and written after the end of the arrays of the calling code for a
  finite strain behaviour and the Cauchy stress); outputs sharing the
  same memory overwrote each other when copied back (only the values of
  a field are now copied back); the field of a group given variable by
  variable was copied although it is ignored;
- SYCL backend: asynchronous computations require an in-order queue. An
  out-of-order queue is synchronized before the kernel;
- documentation of the limits of the shared data (one device per process,
  heap accessible by the device for the backends without device memory).

The comparison program tests empty batches with null fields and invalid
computation options, and uses an in-order SYCL queue.
